{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MacdonaldHookTelescope","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MacdonaldHookTelescope","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.macdonald_hook_telescope_witness_scope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.macdonald_hook_telescope_witness_scope","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L185-L195","doc":"Witness scope tag.  Symbolic verification of\n`macdonald_hook_telescope` was carried out for every partition\nof every `n ∈ {0, 1, …, 6}` — the sum\n`1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 30` records the total number of\n`Z_n` identity instances closed by `sympy.cancel` to `0` and\nrecorded in `y-lambda-macdonald-telescope.witness.json`.\nThe Macdonald-hook closed form was additionally cross-checked\nagainst the MPFR Hoefsmit-matrix witness across 191 samples\nwith maximum absolute deviation `≈ 2.5 · 10⁻⁵¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_closed_form_via_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_closed_form_via_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L154-L181","doc":"**Closed-form $y_\\lambda$ via the telescope**.\n\nFor every partition `λ ⊢ n`, the Jones-Markov coefficient\n`y_λ = s_{λ,X}(Q) / Z_n` collapses (via\n`macdonald_hook_telescope`) to the canonical hook-content form\n\n  y_λ = Q^{n(λ)} · (1 − Q)^n / (1 − X)^n\n          · ∏_{x ∈ λ} (1 − X · Q^{c(x)}) / (1 − Q^{h(x)}).\n\nStated division-free (§7c, the R[h] pattern) as\n`y_λ · Z_n = s_{λ,X}(Q)`; since `Z_n` is a unit this is equivalent to\nthe quotient form `s_{λ,X}(Q) / Z_n = y_λ` quoted above.\n\nThis is `O(n)` per partition (one cell scan for contents and\nhook lengths) — no `sympy.simplify`, no manual algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaClosedForm","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L144-L152","doc":"The clean closed form for `y_λ`: numerator is the Schur\nprincipal-specialisation product, denominator is the telescope.\n\n§7c: dividing by `Z_n = ((1 − X)/(1 − Q))^n` is multiplication by the\nunit `((1 − Q)/(1 − X))^n = (↑v⁻¹ · ↑u)^n`, so the closed form is a\nring element with no field division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlSchurElementValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlSchurElementValue","kind":"axiom","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L138-L142","doc":"Per-partition Wenzl Schur element value, abstracted (full\ndefinition in `y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.macdonald_hook_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.macdonald_hook_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L113-L130","doc":"**Macdonald hook-content telescope**:\n\n  Z_n  =  ((1 - X) / (1 - Q))^n.\n\nProven from the external axiom\n`wenzlNormalizationOfShape_eq_telescope`, which records the\nprincipal specialisation of the regular-representation Frobenius\nidentity (Stanley EC2 Cor. 7.12.5; Macdonald I.3 ex. 1).\n\nVerified symbolically for `n = 0, …, 8` in\n`y_lambda_macdonald_telescope.py`; cross-checked numerically\nagainst `y-lambda-mpfr-witness.json` to ≈ 10⁻⁵¹ over 191\nsamples. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:macdonald-hook-telescope","label":"prop:macdonald-hook-telescope","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlNormalizationOfShape_eq_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlNormalizationOfShape_eq_telescope","kind":"axiom","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L88-L111","doc":"**External axiom (Stanley EC2 Cor. 7.12.5; Macdonald I.3 ex. 1).**\n\nThe regular-representation Frobenius identity\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ n} f_λ · s_λ = p_1^n` together with the principal\nspecialisation `p_1 ↦ (1 − q^r)/(1 − q)` and `X = Q^r` yields the\ntelescope identity for the Wenzl-bridge normalisation.\n\nRecorded as an axiom (per AGENTS.md §3b-cond pattern) since the\nproof depends on the regular-representation Frobenius identity,\nwhich is a deep Mathlib gap pending the symmetric-functions and\nSchur-element infrastructure.  Symbolically verified for `n = 0,\n…, 8` in `y_lambda_macdonald_telescope.py` (sympy.cancel reduces\nthe difference to 0); cross-checked numerically against the MPFR\nHoefsmit-matrix witness with max absolute deviation `≈ 2.5 ·\n10⁻⁵¹` over 191 samples in `y-lambda-mpfr-witness.json`.\n\nThe axiom IS the conjectural input — see §3b-cond audit doc.\n§7c: the old hypothesis `Q ≠ 1` is now the unit witness\n`↑u = 1 − Q`, so the axiom is stated over `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.telescopeRHS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.telescopeRHS","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L84-L86","doc":"The right-hand side of the telescope: a single geometric ratio\n`((1 − X)/(1 − Q))^n`, with `1 − Q` carried as the unit `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlNormalizationOfShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlNormalizationOfShape","kind":"opaque","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/macdonald-hook-telescope.lean#L71-L82","doc":"The Wenzl-bridge normalisation `Z_n = Σ_{λ ⊢ n} f_λ · s_{λ,X}(Q)`,\nabstractly. The sum is encoded by the value `Z_n` on the right of\nthe telescope identity below; this `axiom` records its\nsemantics for downstream lemmas without depending on the full\npartition combinatorics machinery (which lives in\n`y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}